config AVM_ENABLE_BABYTALK_NIFS
    bool "Enable BabyTalk (speech) NIFs"
    default y

config BABYTALK_RESERVE_AT_BOOT
    bool "Reserve the engines' 84.5 KB of internal RAM at boot"
    default y
    depends on AVM_ENABLE_BABYTALK_NIFS
    help
        Transcription and speech need one contiguous 84.5 KB block of internal SRAM, which
        only exists early, before WiFi and the rest fragment the heap: so BabyTalk takes it
        when the VM starts. On a board where that RAM is needed for other things (a display's
        DMA buffers, say) turn this off; an app can then opt in at run time with
        babytalk:reserve_at_boot(true) (NVS namespace "babytalk", key "reserve") and a
        restart. The NVS value, when present, overrides this default either way.

choice BABYTALK_BOARD
    prompt "BabyTalk audio board"
    default BABYTALK_BOARD_WAVESHARE_S3_CAM
    depends on AVM_ENABLE_BABYTALK_NIFS
    help
        Which board_audio.c drives the microphone and speaker. The engines and NIFs are
        board-independent; only board_audio.h's functions touch the hardware.

config BABYTALK_BOARD_WAVESHARE_S3_CAM
    bool "Waveshare ESP32-S3-CAM (ES7210 mics, ES8311 + NS4150B speaker, CH32V003 expander)"

config BABYTALK_BOARD_CUSTOM
    bool "Custom: another component implements board_audio.h"
    help
        board_audio.c is left out; some other component in the firmware (your board's) must
        define every function in board_audio.h. That component can include board_audio.h by
        adding atomvm_babytalk to its REQUIRES.
endchoice
